# CODEOWNERS — paths where a change requires Jon's review before merge.
#
# IMPORTANT: there is NO catch-all `*` owner, intentionally. The auto-merge
# workflow (.github/workflows/auto-merge.yml) relies on CODEOWNERS being
# a narrow "sensitive paths" list, not a repo-wide claim. A `*` owner would
# force Jon's review on every PR once branch protection enables "Require
# review from Code Owners", which defeats the whole triple-gate auto-merge
# design for trivial rollback-safe PRs.
#
# To enforce this file, the repo's branch protection ruleset for `main` and
# `v3/main` must have "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. Without
# that setting the file is advisory only. The auto-label workflow
# (.github/workflows/auto-label-codeowners.yml) also applies
# `needs-jon-approval` on any PR whose diff touches these paths — that
# label is the hard stop for the auto-merge workflow regardless of
# branch-protection enforcement.
#
# When editing this file, also update auto-label-codeowners.yml's regex
# (patterns inlined there because GitHub Actions has no CODEOWNERS parser).
#
# Pattern rules: last-match-wins per file.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Money / prod / legal / auth / CI / supply-chain surfaces.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Database migrations — any change here runs against prod Supabase on deploy.
apps/worker/migrations/**                       @JDC000000

# V3-Y1 training pipeline — data provenance, licenses, and model recipe.
# Everything here touches cease-and-desist defense + the attribution
# contract for the open-source weights release.
/apps/training/                                 @JDC000000

# Scripts — CI invokes several; broadening beyond check_rls.py because a new
# script added here can silently become part of the build or lint path.
scripts/**                                      @JDC000000
# Explicit entry for the Fleet Playbook Move 4 gate — a behavioural script
# that governs PR-body validation, redundant with `scripts/**` above but kept
# so the ownership is obvious at a glance when auditing CI-side policy.
scripts/check_tsd_refs.py                       @JDC000000
# Explicit entry for the Fleet Playbook Move 2 hook — PostToolUse tracer that
# POSTs digest-only events to Langfuse. Redundant with `scripts/**` above but
# called out because a misconfigured trace path could exfil tool metadata; any
# change here deserves explicit review beyond the catch-all.
scripts/langfuse-trace.sh                       @JDC000000

